{"name":"Mouse Trap","hex":"#beb1b0","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"mouse trap","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A device for capturing or killing mice and other rodents.","A website designed to open another copy of itself when the user tries to close the webpage."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To trap; to trick or fool (someone) into a bad situation.","To prevent (the user) from leaving a website by opening another copy when it is closed."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mouse_trap"}],"entries":[{"title":"The Mouse Trap (film)","blocks":[{"text":"The Mouse Trap is a 2024 Canadian comedy slasher film directed, shot and edited by Jamie Bailey and written by Simon Phillips. It is a horror reimagining of Walt Disney's 1928 animated short film Steamboat Willie, the first appearance of Mickey Mouse. The film stars Phillips as a hypnotized manager masked as Mickey, who traps and terrorizes a group of friends inside an amusement arcade."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/64/Mickey%27s_Mouse_Trap_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Mouse_Trap_(film)","wikidata":"Q124098360"},{"title":"Mouse Trap (board game)","blocks":[{"text":"Mouse Trap, originally Mouse Trap Game, is a board game first published by Ideal in 1963 for two to four players. It is one of the first mass-produced three-dimensional board games. Players at first cooperate to build a working mouse trap in the style of a Rube Goldberg machine. Then, players turn against each other to trap opponents' mouse-shaped game pieces."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/5f/Mouse_Trap_Board_and_Box.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mouse_Trap_(board_game)","wikidata":"Q6926039"},{"title":"Mouse Trap (1981 video game)","blocks":[{"text":"Mouse Trap is a maze video game developed by Exidy and released in arcades in 1981. It is similar to Pac-Man, with the main character replaced by a mouse, the dots with cheese, the ghosts with cats, and the energizers with bones. After collecting a bone, pressing a button briefly turns the mouse into a dog. Color-coded doors in the maze can be toggled by pressing a button of the corresponding color. A hawk periodically flies across the maze, unrestricted by walls."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/02/Mouse_Trap_arcade_flyer.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mouse_Trap_(1981_video_game)","wikidata":"Q3326170"},{"title":"Mousetrap","blocks":[{"text":"A mousetrap is a specialized type of animal trap designed primarily to catch and, usually, kill mice. Mousetraps are usually set in an indoor location where there is a suspected infestation of rodents. Larger traps are designed to catch other species of animals, such as rats, squirrels, and other small rodents. Trap types differ significantly in effectiveness, potential harm to wildlife and pets, and the level of suffering caused, with some raising serious welfare and environmental concerns."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Victor-Mousetrap.jpg/330px-Victor-Mousetrap.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mousetrap","wikidata":"Q658353"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/6/64/Mickey%27s_Mouse_Trap_poster.jpg/250px-Mickey%27s_Mouse_Trap_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/64/Mickey%27s_Mouse_Trap_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/6/64/Mickey%27s_Mouse_Trap_poster.jpg/250px-Mickey%27s_Mouse_Trap_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMickey's_Mouse_Trap_poster.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Mickey_Mouse_-_Steamboat_Willie_%281928%29.jpg/500px-Mickey_Mouse_-_Steamboat_Willie_%281928%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Mickey_Mouse_-_Steamboat_Willie_%281928%29.jpg/500px-Mickey_Mouse_-_Steamboat_Willie_%281928%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The original Steamboat Willie version of Mickey Mouse entered into the U.S. public domain in 2024, but any elements that would be unique to later depictions of the character had to be avoided.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMickey_Mouse_-_Steamboat_Willie_(1928).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/5/5f/Mouse_Trap_Board_and_Box.jpg/250px-Mouse_Trap_Board_and_Box.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/5f/Mouse_Trap_Board_and_Box.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/5/5f/Mouse_Trap_Board_and_Box.jpg/250px-Mouse_Trap_Board_and_Box.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMouse_Trap_Board_and_Box.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/US3298692_Mouse_Trap_game_patent_drawings_page-2.png/500px-US3298692_Mouse_Trap_game_patent_drawings_page-2.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/US3298692_Mouse_Trap_game_patent_drawings_page-2.png/1280px-US3298692_Mouse_Trap_game_patent_drawings_page-2